<%# One message. The author and the moment it was written are shown plainly: a
    conversation whose entries are anonymous blocks is not a conversation, and the
    order is the thread's own, which `Discussion#messages` orders. The body is
    markdown, which is rendered as formatted text with support for `**bold**`,
    `# heading`, and `- item` syntax. The thread renders it as such, with no
    sanitizing step because the model handles sanitization at the single entry
    point via `rendered_body`. %>
<li class="discussion-message">
  <%# The author falls back to the shared blank copy rather than rendering an
      empty name. `users.name` is `NOT NULL` and `User` validates its presence, but
      `NOT NULL` rejects only `NULL`, so a direct write or an import can still leave
      an empty string; a message with no visible author is the anonymous block this
      partial exists to avoid. `shared.detail_fact.blank` is the application's
      one answer to "this value is not set", so it is reused instead of a second
      wording invented here.

      The moment is rendered through `l` with a named format, and the machine
      value rides in `datetime`: `%d %b %H:%M` reads as a moment in a
      conversation rather than a date a reader has to interpret, and the
      `datetime` attribute is the exact instant for anything that is not a human
      reading it. %>
  <div class="discussion-message-meta">
    <span class="discussion-message-author"><%= message.user.name.presence || t("shared.detail_fact.blank") %></span>
    <time datetime="<%= message.created_at.iso8601 %>"><%= l message.created_at, format: :short %></time>
  </div>
  <p class="discussion-message-body"><%= message.rendered_body %></p>
</li>
